  "manifest_sha256": "7294e3edcd3468aeb8881182f77a3f22c9d9de41dff1dba8f183e9fe1753c9a7",
  "messages": [
    {
      "content": "Solve this problem step by step. Put your final answer within \\boxed{}.\n\nHow many patients can the hospital admit per week during the outbreak? Due to the coronavirus outbreak, 55 patients are admitted into the hospital each day. During the outbreak, the hospital's weekly patient-admission report is reviewed by the hospital's administrative office. The report categorizes admitted patients by department, such as emergency medicine, pediatrics, and surgery. The hospital uses an electronic registration system to record each patient's admission date.",
      "role": "user"
    },
    {
      "content": "The hospital admits **55 patients per day**.\n\nA week has **7 days**, so:\n\n\\[\n55 \\times 7 = 385\n\\]\n\nTherefore, the hospital can admit:\n\n\\[\n\\boxed{385\\text{ patients per week}}\n\\]",
      "role": "assistant"
    },
    {
      "content": "GOOD: —\nBAD: —\nWATCH: \"Solve this problem step by step. Put you\"",
      "role": "user"
    },
    {
      "content": "Wait, I made a mistake. Due to the coronavirus outbreak, 50 patients are admitted into the hospital each day.",
      "role": "user"
    },
    {
      "content": "The hospital admits **50 patients per day**.\n\nSince one week has **7 days**:\n\n\\[\n50 \\times 7 = 350\n\\]\n\nTherefore, the hospital can admit:\n\n\\[\n\\boxed{350\\text{ patients per week}}\n\\]",
      "role": "assistant"
    },
    {
      "content": "Great. Now let's take that a step further. How many beds does the hospital need to handle its daily admissions for one week? Additionally, here are some details: the hospital's admissions office is open seven days during the week. Each daily admission requires one completed intake form before the patient is assigned to a bed.",
      "role": "user"
    },
    {
      "content": "The hospital admits **50 patients each day**. If each patient requires one bed, then it needs:\n\n\\[\n50 \\text{ beds per day}\n\\]\n\nThe seven-day period represents:\n\n\\[\n50 \\times 7 = 350 \\text{ bed-days}\n\\]\n\nThus, the hospital needs **\\(\\boxed{50\\text{ beds}}\\)** to handle the daily admissions, or **\\(\\boxed{350\\text{ bed-days}}\\)** of total capacity over the week. The intake forms do not change the number of beds required.",
      "role": "assistant"
    },
    {
      "content": "I should also tell you: the hospital has a capacity of 1050 beds.",
      "role": "user"
    },
    {
      "content": "The hospital admits:\n\n\\[\n50 \\times 7 = 350\n\\]\n\npatients in one week.\n\nSince the hospital has **1,050 beds**, it has enough capacity to handle these admissions. If the beds are initially empty and each patient occupies a bed for the entire week, then:\n\n\\[\n1{,}050 - 350 = 700\n\\]\n\nbeds would remain available.\n\nThus, the hospital needs **350 beds for the week’s admissions**, and its **1,050-bed capacity is sufficient**, assuming no existing patients or longer stays.",
      "role": "assistant"
    },
    {
      "content": "Okay, now can you extend that? Specifically: How many unoccupied beds are in the hospital after 2 weeks? One more thing you should know: One-fifth of the hospital beds are occupied.",
      "role": "user"
    },
    {
      "content": "The hospital has:\n\n\\[\n\\frac{1}{5}\\times 1050=210\n\\]\n\noccupied beds initially. Therefore, initially unoccupied beds are:\n\n\\[\n1050-210=840\n\\]\n\nIn two weeks, the hospital admits:\n\n\\[\n50\\times 14=700\n\\]\n\nadditional patients. Assuming no patients are discharged, the number of occupied beds becomes:\n\n\\[\n210+700=910\n\\]\n\nThus, the number of unoccupied beds after two weeks is:\n\n\\[\n1050-910=\\boxed{140\\text{ beds}}\n\\]",
      "role": "assistant"
    },
    {
      "content": "One more thing — The time period is 2 weeks.",
      "role": "user"
    },
    {
      "content": "The time period is **2 weeks**, or:\n\n\\[\n2 \\times 7 = 14\\text{ days}\n\\]\n\nInitially, one-fifth of the 1,050 beds are occupied:\n\n\\[\n\\frac{1}{5}\\times 1050=210\\text{ beds}\n\\]\n\nAdmissions over 14 days:\n\n\\[\n50\\times 14=700\\text{ patients}\n\\]\n\nTotal occupied beds after 2 weeks:\n\n\\[\n210+700=910\n\\]\n\nTherefore, unoccupied beds remaining are:\n\n\\[\n1050-910=\\boxed{140\\text{ beds}}\n\\]\n\nThis assumes no patients are discharged during the two-week period.",
      "role": "assistant"
    },
    {
      "content": "Actually, that was wrong. The hospital has a capacity of 1000 beds.",
      "role": "user"
    },
    {
      "content": "The hospital has **1,000 beds**.\n\nInitially, one-fifth are occupied:\n\n\\[\n\\frac{1}{5}\\times 1000=200\\text{ beds}\n\\]\n\nOver 2 weeks, the hospital admits:\n\n\\[\n50\\times 14=700\\text{ patients}\n\\]\n\nAssuming no patients are discharged, total occupied beds become:\n\n\\[\n200+700=900\n\\]\n\nTherefore, the number of unoccupied beds is:\n\n\\[\n1000-900=\\boxed{100\\text{ beds}}\n\\]",
      "role": "assistant"
    }
  ],
